    "# Chapter 1 — TD-PINNs: Time-Integrator Comparison (fixed epochs)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Case:** 1-D viscous Burgers, sawtooth analytic solution (Hopf–Cole) on $[0, 2\\pi]$, spatial operator\n",
    "$S(u) \\equiv u\\,u_x - \\nu\\,u_{xx}$ (so the PDE is $u_t + S(u) = 0$).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** keep the **native `PINTrainer`** (TD-PINNs, MLP, fixed uniform collocation) and vary *only* the\n",
    "time integrator. The integrator is **not** a trainer setting — it lives entirely in the residual\n",
    "function (the loss function). The trainer hands the residual a `u_prev` that keeps its graph w.r.t. $x$,\n",
    "so a residual can differentiate the frozen previous step when it needs to:\n",
    "\n",
    "| integrator | residual $R$ (we minimise $\\langle R^2\\rangle$) | $S$ from |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Explicit Euler** | $\\dfrac{u-u^{t-1}}{\\Delta t} + S(u^{t-1})$ | frozen $t{-}1$ |\n",
    "| **Implicit Euler** | $\\dfrac{u-u^{t-1}}{\\Delta t} + S(u)$ | current $t$ (AD) |\n",
    "| **Crank–Nicolson** | $\\dfrac{u-u^{t-1}}{\\Delta t} + \\tfrac12\\big[S(u) + S(u^{t-1})\\big]$ | half / half |\n",
    "\n",
    "The Crank–Nicolson residual is the requested scheme:\n",
    "$\\frac{u^{t}-u^{t-1}}{\\Delta t} = \\tfrac12[(\\nu u_{xx}^{t-1} - u^{t-1}u_x^{t-1}) + (\\nu u_{xx}^{t} - u^{t}u_x^{t})]$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What is different in this variant:** the number of **epochs is fixed** (no early stopping —\n",
    "`TOLERANCE = 0`, so every step runs the full budget). Each integrator is summarised as a single point\n",
    "whose **horizontal axis is the training loss reached** at that fixed budget, and whose vertical axis is\n",
    "the error vs the analytical solution. Lower-left = lower loss *and* lower error for the same number of\n",
    "epochs."
   ]
  },
