    "  and does lower loss translate into lower $L_\\infty$ error? A method sitting lower-left wins on both.\n",
    "- The integrator still lives entirely in the `loss_fn` (the residual); the trainer is unchanged.\n",
    "- Explicit Euler carries the explicit scheme's CFL sensitivity; Crank–Nicolson is $O(\\Delta t^2)$ and\n",
    "  usually most accurate at the same `DT`."
